  "content": {
    "id": "p11-q6-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "6",
    "prompt": "A triangle has base length 4 cm greater than its height. If the area of the triangle is $48\\text{ cm}^2$, find the height of the triangle.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$8\\text{ cm}$",
      "worked": "Let $h$ cm be the height. The base is $(h+4)$ cm.\n\nUsing the triangle area formula:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac12h(h+4)&=48\\\\h(h+4)&=96\\\\h^2+4h-96&=0\\\\(h+12)(h-8)&=0\\\\h&=-12\\text{ or }h=8\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe height must be positive, so the triangle has height $8\\text{ cm}$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 62
  },
